 {"id":"fabro-6b58","title":"Bound the planner in-flight check: created_since window plus explicit self-exclusion","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T17:13:54.681Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T17:32:22.037Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 4 (IN-FLIGHT PR CHECK): call fabro_runs_list with created_since ≈ 48 h, and add one line telling the planner to exclude this run's own id (from its preamble header) from the in-flight set. Grounded in run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA: the unbounded call (event seq 41) returned 16 runs / 14,492 bytes — 15 terminal with identical generic goal text — and the planner had to deduce 'the only non-terminal run is this run itself'. Verified regression: closed seed fabro-9967 mandated created_since but the current prompt text carries no such bound. Expected effect: tool output drops ~14.5 KB to ≤2 KB per run and the self-run confusion class disappears. Basis: run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA, workflow version 70cee3b32d01c25022b0c84ba4b42f2e8c93d679f400542db4ca1cafafa1a6c1, commit 515758e102a81c1c35d8c41bb3fd96209f1f04e9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d4c","title":"Planner prompt: probe file structure with heading greps, never head -N full files","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T17:13:59.032Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T17:32:22.217Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 3 (stale-basis verification): add 'Probe structure with grep -n \"^#\" <file> and ls <dir>, never head -N full files.' Grounded in run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA: one basis probe (head -40 AGENTS.md plus greps, event seq 51–53) pulled 4,677 bytes into context to answer a question about section headings, burning ~12 s re-proving layout facts the just-merged Dev-loop assets map (seed fabro-3d2d) already settles. Expected effect: ~4 KB less context and fewer probe calls per run; distinct from open fabro-9fa2 (fast path for pinned line anchors), which triggers on a different condition. Basis: run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA, workflow version 70cee3b32d01c25022b0c84ba4b42f2e8c93d679f400542db4ca1cafafa1a6c1, commit 515758e102a81c1c35d8c41bb3fd96209f1f04e9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-7808","title":"Implementer prompt: state that grep exit 1 on pre-change verification is an expected no-match","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T17:14:04.379Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T17:32:22.136Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md verification section, add one line: 'grep exit 1 = no match; on pre-change verification that is the expected state, not an error.' Grounded in run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA: the implementer's first shell call exited 1 and was flagged is_error: true (event seq 97–98) only because grep 'Dev-loop assets' AGENTS.md found nothing before the section existed — harmless here, but it trains the model to read exit 1 as failure, and run history records a prior 'sandbox rg unreliable' misdiagnosis from the same benign signal. Expected effect: removes a recurring false-error signal and prevents misdiagnosis loops; orthogonal to open fabro-a23f (journal reporting of errored calls). Basis: run 01M23HWFFSB9NK78PGSCZWE6MA, workflow version 70cee3b32d01c25022b0c84ba4b42f2e8c93d679f400542db4ca1cafafa1a6c1, commit 515758e102a81c1c35d8c41bb3fd96209f1f04e9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
